      "question_type": "mcq",
      "rationale": "12 / 0.02 = 600 pieces.",
      "explanation": "7,200 kg/m³ is too low; would under‑estimate weight. 7,500 kg/m³ is close but is not the standard value. 8,000 kg/m³ is slightly high; may be used for heavier alloys. Steel density is 7,850 kg/m³, which is encoded in the formula denominator (162.5). Standard structural steel density = 7,850 kg/m³. This is fundamental to rebar weight calculations.",
